{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "The Last Curtain of Lantern Hall",
  "summary": "Lantern Marionette Theater, a solar-vine playhouse, was holding its Bloom Jubilee, the yearly celebration of the troupe that taught its puppets to move without strings. Decades of neglected maintenance let the living roof rot and its biolight grids dim, but the town gathered anyway for one last show. Moments ago, as the finale began, the old stage-vine seized up and the puppets rose on their own, all turning to face the audience. The crowd fled mid-song, leaving warm cups, spilled petals, and a stage still humming. The player pieces together that the puppeteers never controlled the show at the end; the puppets have been performing for an audience that left them behind.",
